====================================================================================================
External services (not bundled)
====================================================================================================

HyperLevel talks to these programs over their HTTP APIs only. No code of theirs is included in this
repository or in the HyperLevel Docker image; each runs as its own service under its own license.

- OpenShorts (https://github.com/mutonby/openshorts) – MIT License. Optional engine behind the
  Video-Studio; deploy/openshorts/ and the "openshorts" profile in docker-compose.yml build the
  upstream image from its own repository.
- Postiz (https://github.com/gitroomhq/postiz-app) – AGPL-3.0. Optional engine behind the Social
  Planner, self-hosted separately.
- Hosted APIs you may connect with your own credentials (Anthropic, OpenAI, Stripe, Twilio, Meta,
  Google, Microsoft, Todoist, HubSpot, Supabase, ElevenLabs …) are governed by their providers'
  terms.

- Office editors and engines (docs/office.md) – WordCraft, GridCraft, DeckCraft and PdfCraft by the ArtCraft Team
  (https://github.com/storytold), each MIT OR Apache-2.0. Optional: deploy/office/ downloads their pinned release files
  (browser WebAssembly builds and command-line programs) at install time; HyperLevel talks to them through files, command lines
  and postMessage only. Attribution, license text and the trademark note: deploy/office/THIRD-PARTY.md. Their names and logos
  are trademarks of the ArtCraft Team and are not used in HyperLevel's interface.

- integrations/zapier/ declares zapier-platform-core as its dependency; it is installed by whoever
  builds and pushes the Zapier app (`npm install && npx zapier push`) and is not distributed here.

